> [!IMPORTANT]
> Depends on this docs-infra PR: https://github.com/mui/mui-public/pull/1109

I think a `Private` tag sounds nice. I think it mirrors OOP terms `public`, `protected`, `private` methods.

I think we should avoid `unstable-` in the path because then links will change when it becomes stable. I like the approach of the Drawer component that simply renames the export to `DrawerPreview`:

https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/bb9a81054729e44a6eb4110e64ffedea4d660751/packages/react/src/drawer/index.ts#L1

With a note at the top:

https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/bb9a81054729e44a6eb4110e64ffedea4d660751/docs/src/app/(docs)/react/components/drawer/page.mdx?plain=1#L11

That way the types change, but the URL stays stable. Then we could progress `/react/components/calendar` Private -> Preview -> Stable phases

We can hide it from navigation and search by adding a `filter` function to `createSitemap()` here:

https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/master/docs/src/app/sitemap/index.ts

```ts
export const sitemap = createSitemap(
  import.meta.url,
  {
    Overview,
    Handbook,
    Components,
    Utils,
  },
  {
    filter: (page) => !page.tags?.includes('Private') || process.env.DEPLOY_ENV !== 'production',
  },
);
```

Then update this to `[Private]`

https://github.com/flaviendelangle/base-ui/blob/c66b089985d03678fa80bd9738254ce275a30213/docs/src/app/(docs)/react/components/page.mdx?plain=1#L10

